ication question, \\\"Translate print(1 + 2) from Python to JavaScript\\\" returns a fragment of the prompt, and a request to add a JSDoc comment to a named function makes no change. A rename of a function is handled correctly (see the gist).\\n\\nFound while trying formal-ai on small tasks from https://github.com/link-foundation/universal-translator (see https://github.com/link-foundation/universal-translator/issues/14). Full transcripts: https://gist.github.com/konard/0d942b7c1c3a9cdd96519eaf142e591e\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- formal-ai 0.357.2 (release binary `formal-ai-cli-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl`; source commit b9b4a0a52), Linux x86_64\\n- `formal-ai chat --prompt ...`, `formal-ai translate`, and (for the JSDoc task) `formal-ai serve --agent-mode` with an OpenAI tool loop (`drive.py` in the gist)\\n\\n## Reproduction and results\\n\\n```bash\\nformal-ai chat --prompt \\\"Write a JavaScript function that returns the sum of squares of an array.\\\"\\nformal-ai chat --prompt \\\"Write a JavaScript function that returns the sum of squares of an array of numbers.\\\"\\nformal-ai chat --prompt \\\"Write a function sumOfSquares(arr) in JavaScript\\\"\\nformal-ai chat --prompt \\\"Translate print(1 + 2) from Python to JavaScript.\\\"\\nformal-ai chat --prompt \\\"Translate this Python code to JavaScript: print(1 + 2)\\\"\\nformal-ai chat --prompt \\\"Convert print(1 + 2) from Python into JavaScript\\\"\\nformal-ai translate --from python --to js --input p.js\\necho 'console.log(1 + 2);' > p.js && formal-ai translate --from js --to rust --input p.js\\n# agent mode, workspace containing examples/universal-app/src/editor-sync.js:\\npython3 -I drive.py \\\"Add a JSDoc comment to the function scrollToPosition in editor-sync.js\\\"\\n```\\n\\n| Prompt | Actual | Expected |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Write a JS function ... sum of squares of an array (2 phrasings) | `Which integer range should the program use?` | `function sumOfSquares(values) { return values.reduce((t, v) => t + v * v, 0); }` |\\n| Write a function sumOfSquares(arr) in JavaScript | `I cannot write this program: no synthesis route reaches task \\\"sumOfSquares\\\" in language \\\"javascript\\\"` | same function (the refusal is honest, but a fold over an array is the most basic idiom) |\\n| Translate print(1 + 2) from Python to JavaScript. | `\\\"print(1 + 2) from Python\\\"` | `console.log(1 + 2);` |\\n| Translate this Python code to JavaScript: print(1 + 2) | `\\\"this Python code\\\"` | `console.log(1 + 2);` |\\n| Convert print(1 + 2) from Python into JavaScript | `Fused 0 statement(s) from 0 captured source(s) ...` (empty) | `console.log(1 + 2);` |\\n| translate --from python --to js | `unknown --from 'python': expected one of rust, js, ts, or meta` | Python is a language of the project's own meta-language family; at least a clear \\\"not supported\\\" in chat |\\n| translate --from js --to rust (input `console.log(1 + 2);`) | prints the input unchanged: `console.log(1 + 2);` (listed as `js -> rust live`) | Rust such as `println!(\\\"{}\\\", 1 + 2);`, or an explicit \\\"not translatable\\\" |\\n| Add a JSDoc comment to scrollToPosition in editor-sync.js (also \\\"Document ... with a JSDoc comment\\\", \\\"Add a JSDoc comment above function ... describing its parameters\\\") | `What exact text should go into editor-sync.js, and where? ...`, or `Left editor-sync.js unchanged: it already has content, and the request does not say to replace the whole file.` | a `/** ... @param ... */` block inserted above `export function scrollToPosition(editor, position)` (the function already has a plain `//` comment that can seed the description) |\\n\\nPassing control: \\\"Rename the function foldChanges to foldingChanges in editor-sync.js\\\" is done with `perl -pi -e 's/\\\\bfoldChanges\\\\b/foldingChanges/g'` and both occurrences change (lines 113 and 261); the file still passes `node --check`.\\n\\n## Likely cause (from reading the source; not stepped through a debugger)\\n\\n- \\\"Which integer range\\\" is the clarification in `data/seed/coding-guidance.lino` line 269; the request is routed to an integer-range program family because of the words \\\"sum\\\"/\\\"array\\\"/\\\"function\\\", before any array-of-numbers reading. The clarification is not about anything in the prompt.\\n- The translation phrase \\\"Translate X from A to B\\\" is read as a definition/extraction request and the quoted answer is the noun phrase before \\\"from\\\"; the language pair (Python -> JavaScript) is never extracted, so the existing `translate` machinery (`formal-ai translate`, `rust/src/` meta-language translation, plan 16 L2) is not reached. `translate` itself accepts only rust|js|ts|meta, and `js -> rust` echoes input.\\n- The \\\"What exact text should go...\\\" refusal is `data/seed/multilingual-responses-agentic-tools.lino` line 585, produced by the literal-addition guard (`rust/src/agentic_coding/literal_addition.rs` / `literal_write_guard.rs`): additions must be quoted. Documentation requests whose text is derivable from the function (name, parameters, existing comment) are not generated, although `rust/src/agentic_coding/source_documentation.rs` exists.\\n\\n## Workaround\\n\\n- Quote the code: \\\"Append ... \\\" with the literal text; or give the target text to the model (\\\"Replace the two comment lines above scrollToPosition with: /** ... */\\\").\\n- For translation, use the project's own CLI: `formal-ai translate --from js --to ts --input file` (only rust/js/ts/meta).\\n- For rename, plain prompts work.\\n\\n## Suggested fix\\n\\n1. Add an extraction step for `translate/convert <code> from <language A> to/into <language B>` in the chat intent layer that binds `(source language, target language, code)`, and hands them to the meta-language translation (the same path as `formal-ai translate`); when a language is unsupported, say so instead of echoing a fragment. Add Python as a reader at least for `print`/arithmetic/function statements.\\n2. Make `formal-ai translate --from js --to rust` fail loudly (or return Rust) when the program cannot be emitted; today identity output is indistinguishable from success.\\n3. For \\\"function that returns <fold> of an array\\\", add idiom entries (sum, product, sum of squares, max, count) to the `seed_idiom_composer` route named in the refusal, and do not ask for an integer range when the prompt names an array.\\n4. In the literal-addition guard, treat \\\"add a JSDoc/docstring/comment to <function>\\\" as a derivable edit: take name, parameters (from the declaration) and the preceding comment, and generate the block (`source_documentation.rs`). Keep the question only when nothing can be derived.\\n\\n\\n__formal_ai_exit=0\\n\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Let me take the next step to handle that for you.\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call_a7af758da75b24f5\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"glob\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/p.js\\\"}\"}}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call_a7af758da75b24f5\",\"content\":\"No files found\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Let me open /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1795661355081/examples/universal-app/src/editor-sync.js and read what it says.\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call_3d7980b0022b7e80\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"read\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1795661355081/examples/universal-app/src/editor-sync.js\\\"}\"}}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call_3d7980b0022b7e80\",\"content\":\"Error: File not found: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1795661355081/examples/universal-app/src/editor-sync.js\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Let me take the next step to handle that for you.\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call_125daf6734ab1a3c\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"glob\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/editor-sync.js\\\"}\"}}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call_125daf6734ab1a3c\",\"content\":\"No files found\"},{\"role\